From ab0b99a211e3a9dbf5f0796b8a7cb1965862fe35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:23:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/58] dt-bindings: iommu: apple,sart: Add the T6050 SART

The T6050 (M5 Ultra) SART keeps SARTv3's entries but moves the address
and size arrays, so it is not compatible with apple,t6000-sart and has
no fallback.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,sart.yaml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,sart.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,sart.yaml
index e6482453d6da..19ffe1bf167f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,sart.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,sart.yaml
@@ -26,6 +26,9 @@ description:
   SART3, first seen in M1 Pro/Max, extends both the address space and filter
   entry size to 42 bit.
 
+  SART4, seen on M5 Ultra (T6050), keeps SART3's entries but moves the
+  address and size arrays, so it has no SART3 fallback.
+
 properties:
   compatible:
     oneOf:
@@ -43,6 +46,7 @@ properties:
           - const: apple,t6000-sart
       - enum:
           - apple,t6000-sart
+          - apple,t6050-sart
           - apple,t8015-sart
           - apple,t8103-sart
 
